 "title": "What to ask before discounting your offer",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains what to ask a prospect when they request a discount. The main lesson is to ensure price is the only obstacle before offering a price reduction.",
 "key_points": [
  "When somebody asks for a discount, start with this question.",
  "Ask: Outside of money, are you aligned on everything else?",
  "Explain what that means: If I can solve money for you, are you ready to move forward with me right now?",
  "If they are not aligned on everything else, there is no point in offering a discount.",
  "Otherwise, the prospect will just find another excuse."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: Ask this before you Discount your offer! Video by saadsells.value. Transcript: When somebody asks for a discount, you always want to start with this. Okay, you want a discount? Not a problem. Outside of money, are you aligned on everything else? What that means is, if I can solve money for you, are you ready to move forward with me right now? Now, if they are not, then there's no point in offering a discount. Otherwise, he'll just find another excuse. On-screen text: Ask this before you Discount your offer!",
